; AmiBroker ASCII import format: IDX bars + frequency, turnover and net foreign flow.
;
; Column order MUST match export-amibroker.js exportIdx():
;   Ticker, YYYY-MM-DD, Open, High, Low, Close, Volume, Frequency, Turnover, Aux1, Aux2
;
; WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE FORMAT FILE
; The US and GLOBAL bars carry no frequency, turnover or foreign flow. Reusing this format
; there would write a column of zeros into AUX1/AUX2, and AmiBroker cannot distinguish
; "no foreign trading" from "nobody measured it" - a flat AUX1 line would read as a real
; market statement. Each source keeps its own format instead.
;
; WHAT AUX1/AUX2 HOLD
;   AUX1 = net foreign flow in SHARES (foreign_buy - foreign_sell), signed.
;   AUX2 = 1 when the exchange published foreign flow for that bar, 0 when it did not.
;
; WHY AUX2 IS A FLAG AND NOT A RATIO
; AmiBroker stores AUX as a plain float with no null. An empty field, a missing field and a
; literal 0 all read back as 0, so AUX1 alone cannot distinguish "foreign traders netted zero"
; from "IDX published nothing" - and for 47,803 of 167,472 real IDX bars in 2026 it published
; nothing. Without the flag every 52-week foreign average is dragged toward zero by bars that
; carry no information. In AFL:  ok = Aux2 > 0;  net = IIf(ok, Aux1, 0);
; AUX1 is raw shares, exactly as the exchange reports it, so it lines up with Volume. It is
; deliberately NOT multiplied by price: prices in this file are corporate-action adjusted,
; so a split would silently rescale every historical flow figure. A share count does not move
; when a split happens and the split factor does not affect it.
;
; Volume is split+dividend adjusted by the exporter (that is what the chart needs), so Volume
; and AUX1 are on different bases for the 173 codes in ca_factors. For the other 800+ codes
; nothing was adjusted and both are raw. Do not compute AUX1/Volume as "foreign share of
; trading" without checking ca_factors first.
;
; FREQUENCY AND TURNOVER CANNOT BE IMPORTED
; $FORMAT accepts Frequency and Turnover without complaint and then DISCARDS them: a test row
; carrying Volume, Frequency, Turnover, AUX1, AUX2 came back with Frequency and Turnover gone,
; AmiBroker's OpenInt was 0, and the importer had shifted AUX1 into the Frequency slot. Verified
; against AmiBroker 6.30, not inferred from the docs. Frequency is therefore not in this file at
; all; if it is needed it has to go through OpenInt (the one 10-column layout that read back
; correctly), which this format deliberately does not do - a trading frequency in a field named
; OpenInterest misleads every AFL script that reads OI for futures.

$FORMAT Ticker,Date_YMD,Open,High,Low,Close,Volume,AUX1,AUX2
$SEPARATOR ,
$SKIPLINES 0
$AUTOADD 1
$BREAKONERR 1
$DEBUG 1
